  "body": "## Summary\nPer Owner directive UMR-20260801-142246-8d51 (corrected by UMR-20260801-142419-d82a to first evaluate existing engines): closes the real duplicate-work-incident gap (3 near-duplicate PR-58-conflict-fix attempts in projexa, plus a build-extend-*-track-engines dispatch storm found during today's PR-backlog audit) by making \"what already exists / who's touching what / what depends on what\" queryable instead of requiring a manual `ACTIVE-CLAIMS.yaml` read.\n\n**Engine-coverage investigation done first** (see commit message / PR discussion): checked the real, verified `ai-os/generated/engine_inventory_2026-07-24.yaml` catalog. Knowledge Engine's `entity_relationships` is a free-text JSON blob on code/doc artifacts only (no relation table, no recursive query). Wiring Engine's entity/relation concept is scoped to code-wiring (function/route/table). `task_claims`/`claim-task-key` is exact-string task_key dedup only. None cover a typed claims/addresses/depends_on/implemented_by/conflicts_with graph across task/pr/issue/file_area/agent/report/engine — confirmed as a real, unbuilt gap.\n\n## What's added\n- `entity`/`relation` tables in `superboss-register.py`'s existing SQLite DB (get-or-create idempotent on `entity` via `UNIQUE(type,key)`; append-only `relation` edges). Wired into both `init_db()` and `_migrate_schema()` so the live production DB picks this up automatically on its next call.\n- `log-entity`/`log-relation` CLI subcommands (mirrors `log-instruction`/`log-work`).\n- `check-conflict`: a real `WITH RECURSIVE` SQL query — finds other open task/pr entities with a `claims` edge into an overlapping `file_area` (path-prefix match) for the same or a *related* issue (transitively via `depends_on`/`implemented_by` edges).\n- `backfill_active_claims.py`: migrates `compliance-tracker/ai-os/boss/ACTIVE-CLAIMS.yaml`'s real entries in (171 task entities, 639 claims relations from real data). Found and worked around one real pre-existing YAML indentation bug in that file.\n- Wired into `dispatch-owner-task.sh` (warn-only conflict check before registering a new task, plus logging the new task's own claim so the graph stays current) and a standalone `check-conflict-before-pr.sh` for the \"before opening a PR\" point (no single centralized PR-open script exists in this codebase to hook automatically).\n\nWarning-only throughout — never blocks, per the directive's own explicit instruction.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `log-entity` idempotency: re-logging the same (type, key) returns the same `entity_id`\n- [x] `check-conflict` positive match (exact + prefix-overlapping file_area), negative match (unrelated file_area), negative match (unrelated issue)\n- [x] Transitive related-issue traversal via a `depends_on` edge (recursive CTE)\n- [x] `closed`/`merged`/`abandoned` status correctly excluded from conflict results\n- [x] Real backfill run against the actual `ACTIVE-CLAIMS.yaml` (171/171 entries, 639 relations) into a scratch DB — never the live one\n- [x] Migration path verified against a simulated pre-existing (old-schema) DB — new tables appear after the first call, no data loss\n- [x] Regression check: `log-instruction`/`log-work`/`search`/`claim-task-key`/`check-task-key` all still work unchanged\n- [x] `dispatch-owner-task.sh` and `check-conflict-before-pr.sh` both syntax-checked (`bash -n`) and exercised end-to-end against a scratch DB\n\nAll testing done against scratch/test databases via `SUPERBOSS_REGISTER_DB` env override — the live production database was never touched by this branch's development.",
